  "id": "ksabwriterswing",
  "neon": "#b98cff",
  "note": "KSAB WRITERS' WING — the broadcaster's annex on Marrow Street. A two-storey glass pavilion\nunder one deep floating roof slab, with the stair core expressed as a full-height glazed drum on\nthe street corner and a clerestory box above the roof plane.\n\n⚠ NO AERIAL. A mast and a roof board both want the middle of the same small deck, and `signfit`\ncounted one drawing across the other at three headings out of four; moving either only changed\nwhich headings it spoiled. The transmitter belongs to the KSAB-TV stage one tile south anyway.\nWriters do not need one.\n\n⚠ THE ROOF SLAB IS WIDER THAN THE GLASS UNDER IT, which is the entire read: a modern pavilion is\na floor plane and a roof plane with nothing structural in between, and the only way to say that\nhere is to set the glazed box back and let the slab oversail it. The body is therefore 0.40/0.33\nand the slab is 0.435.\n\n⚠ THE BODY IS A CENTRED NON-SQUARE BOX, which is legal where an OFF-CENTRE one would not be — a\ncentred footprint cannot rotate out from under itself, so its radial reach is the same at all four\nentrance facings. That is what lets this building be shallower than it is wide.",
